821:
(a) No tent sale vendor shall sell and deliver at the time of sale any article to the buyer without having first made application for a license to do business, which application shall recite:
(1) The name of the vendor;
(2) The name of the agent conducting the sale, if any;
(3) The place where the sale is to be conducted;
(4) A signed copy of site use authorization from property owner;
(5) The hours of sale; and
(6) The number of days during which the sale is to be conducted.
(b) The application shall be accompanied by an application fee in the amount of twenty-five dollars ($25.00) and a copy of a current Georgia occupation tax permit held by the party wishing to hold such tent sale.
(c) If issued, a permit will require the payment of a fee in the amount of one hundred dollars ($100.00) per day for the duration of the tent sale.
(d) The following restrictions shall apply to all tent sales, except for tent sales of fireworks:
(1) The tent used must be a minimum of six hundred (600) square feet;
(2) The tent sale shall only last for a maximum of five (5) consecutive days;
(3) There must be at least forty-five (45) calendar days between a single business' tent sales;
(4) Merchandise sold at the tent sale must be the merchandise as sold in the business location;
(5) The tent sale may only be located either on the parcel in which the business is located or within one hundred (100) feet of such parcel.
(e) Any person who shall undertake to do business as a tent sales vendor without having complied with the terms of this article or who shall make any false statements in any application for such a permit shall be guilty of an offense.
(f) Fines for such offense shall the maximum provided in the applicable section of the City Code and each day shall be deemed a separate offense.
(Ord. No. 51-03, § 1, 7-21-03; Ord. No. 09-17, § 1, 3-6-17)

836:
